      "gruppe": "B",
      "recap_tekst": "Switzerland beat Canada 2-1.\nGoals: Switzerland — Vargas (46) and Manzambi (57); Canada — Promise David (76).\n\nSwitzerland advance to the Round of 32 after Juan Vargas and Johan Manzambi earned victory over co-hosts Canada, who also punched their ticket.\nCo-hosts Canada’s party at the FIFA World Cup 2026™ will continue through the knockout stages - though it was Switzerland celebrating the loudest in Vancouver after a hard-fought victory secured first place in Group B for Murat Yakin’s men.\nWhile both teams march on - Canada for the first time in their history - Switzerland’s success, achieved through second-half strikes by Juan Vargas and Johan Manzambi, means they will be back at BC Place Vancouver on 2 July to take on the third-placed team from Group E, F, G, I or J in the Round of 32.\nKey stat: Switzerland have qualified from the group stage for the sixth time in their last seven World Cup campaigns.",
